---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
const feedUrl = 'https://hardeepanand.com/rss.xml';
const emailSubject = encodeURIComponent('Follow The Systems Lens');
const emailBody = encodeURIComponent('Please add me to The Systems Lens update list.');
---
<Base title="Follow Updates" description="Follow new Systems Lens essays by email request or RSS reader app." active="/writing/">
  <section class="follow-page">
    <div class="follow-hero">
      <span class="follow-kicker">FOLLOW THE SYSTEMS LENS</span>
      <h1>New essays, without another social feed.</h1>
      <p>There are two useful ways to keep up: ask to be notified directly, or use RSS if you already read through an app like Feedly, NetNewsWire, Readwise Reader, Outlook, or a similar reader.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="follow-grid" aria-label="Ways to follow">
      <article class="follow-card">
        <span class="follow-number">01</span>
        <h2>Ask to be notified</h2>
        <p>Best for people who want a human follow-up path. It keeps the relationship direct and avoids turning the site into a comment feed or reaction system.</p>
        <a href={`mailto:hardeep@apas.ai?subject=${emailSubject}&body=${emailBody}`}>Email Hardeep →</a>
      </article>
      <article class="follow-card">
        <span class="follow-number">02</span>
        <h2>Use RSS in a reader app</h2>
        <p>RSS is a machine-readable list of new published essays. The raw page looks technical in a browser because it is meant for reader apps, not humans.</p>
        <a href="/rss.xml">Open the RSS feed →</a>
      </article>
      <article class="follow-card">
        <span class="follow-number">03</span>
        <h2>Browse the library</h2>
        <p>The writing library is the clean human version: articles, topics, reading paths, and visual guides without needing any separate app.</p>
        <a href="/writing/">Go to all essays →</a>
      </article>
    </div>
    <section class="rss-explainer" aria-labelledby="rss-heading">
      <div>
        <span class="follow-kicker">WHAT RSS DOES</span>
        <h2 id="rss-heading">The feed is plumbing. The reader app is the interface.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="rss-steps">
        <div><strong>Copy the feed link</strong><span>{feedUrl}</span></div>
        <div><strong>Add it to a reader app</strong><span>The app checks for new essays automatically.</span></div>
        <div><strong>Read updates in one inbox</strong><span>No algorithm, no comments, no noisy timeline.</span></div>
      </div>
      <p>For The Systems Lens, RSS is valuable because it keeps serious readers close to the work without depending on LinkedIn, email deliverability, or a public social platform. It also gives APAS a clean future integration point for newsletters, knowledge capture, and the living-brain content pipeline.</p>
    </section>
  </section>
</Base>
<style>
.follow-page{width:min(1120px,calc(100% - 64px));margin:0 auto;padding:76px 0 20px}.follow-hero{max-width:760px}.follow-kicker{font:700 10px/1.5 var(--font-body);letter-spacing:.14em;color:var(--publication-gold)}.follow-hero h1{font:400 72px/1.02 var(--font-display);letter-spacing:-.03em;margin:18px 0}.follow-hero p{font:18px/1.8 var(--font-body);color:var(--text-dim);max-width:62ch}.follow-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,minmax(0,1fr));gap:18px;margin-top:50px}.follow-card{border:1px solid color-mix(in srgb,var(--line) 80%,var(--publication-gold) 20%);background:color-mix(in srgb,var(--bg) 92%,var(--publication-gold) 8%);padding:24px;min-height:280px;display:flex;flex-direction:column}.follow-number{font:700 10px/1.4 var(--font-body);letter-spacing:.12em;color:var(--publication-gold)}.follow-card h2{font:400 31px/1.08 var(--font-display);margin:22px 0 12px}.follow-card p{font:14px/1.75 var(--font-body);color:var(--text-dim);margin:0 0 24px}.follow-card a{margin-top:auto;color:var(--text);text-decoration:none;font:600 13px/1.5 var(--font-body)}.rss-explainer{display:grid;grid-template-columns:.82fr 1.18fr;gap:44px;border-block:1px solid var(--line);margin-top:56px;padding:42px 0}.rss-explainer h2{font:400 42px/1.08 var(--font-display);margin:14px 0 0}.rss-steps{display:grid;gap:12px}.rss-steps div{border-left:3px solid var(--publication-gold);padding:12px 0 12px 18px}.rss-steps strong{display:block;font:600 13px/1.5 var(--font-body)}.rss-steps span,.rss-explainer p{display:block;font:14px/1.75 var(--font-body);color:var(--text-dim);word-break:break-word}.rss-explainer p{grid-column:2;margin:8px 0 0;max-width:68ch}@media(max-width:850px){.follow-page{width:calc(100% - 40px);padding-top:48px}.follow-hero h1{font-size:48px}.follow-grid,.rss-explainer{grid-template-columns:1fr}.rss-explainer p{grid-column:1}.follow-card{min-height:0}}
</style>
